cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NRAG in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "NRAG: Compiled Retrieval — embedding-free RAG"
authors:
  - family-names: "Natthanarong"
    given-names: "Nine"
repository-code: "https://github.com/NineNatthanarong/NRAG"
url: "https://github.com/NineNatthanarong/NRAG"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - retrieval
  - RAG
  - BM25
  - sparse-retrieval
  - embedding-free
  - information-retrieval
abstract: >-
  NRAG compiles documents once with an LLM into an enriched, purely lexical index
  (contextual blurbs, doc2query questions, propositions, reasoning expansions, and
  consensus-weighted sparse terms); every query afterwards is pure BM25 — no embedding
  model, no vector database, no GPU, at zero marginal query cost.
